    "content": "<h1>README</h1>\n<h1>🎯 Seller Acquisition Strategy — Overview & Roadmap</h1>\n<h2>PAGE INFORMATION</h2>\n<li><strong>Page Name:</strong> Seller Acquisition Strategy — Topic Overview</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Provide an overarching strategic framework detailing who we acquire, where we find them, how we prioritize categories, and our conversion goals.</li>\n<li><strong>Section:</strong> 3. 🎯 Seller Acquisition Strategy</li>\n<h2>Overview</h2>\n<p>A high-performing acquisition engine is guided by deliberate strategy rather than random outreach. The <strong>Seller Acquisition Strategy</strong> section outlines Vipto’s targeting parameters, geographic expansion clusters, merchant qualification models, channel priorities, and conversion funnel definitions for onboarding local retailers onto our product discovery network.</p>\n<h2>Why This Matters</h2>\n<p>If our 11-person team reaches out to random shops across a 50 km radius in 30 disconnected categories, we create a fragmented, low-density marketplace where customers find few relevant options in their neighborhood. A focused strategy builds dense, high-liquidity merchant clusters in key shopping districts, allowing nearby customers to discover products and confirm stock easily.</p>\n<h2>Objectives</h2>\n<li>Understand Vipto’s acquisition targets across key neighborhood retail clusters.</li>\n<li>Master the Target Seller Profile (TSP) and qualification criteria for local physical stores.</li>\n<li>Learn our category hierarchy (electronics, fashion, mobile, sports, gifts, stationery, grocery, medical).</li>\n<li>Understand our geographic clustering strategy (pin codes and commercial high streets).</li>\n<li>Execute the 6-stage seller acquisition funnel with high precision.</li>\n<h2>How It Works</h2>\n<p>Our acquisition strategy connects five strategic pillars:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">Target Seller Profile (TSP) ──► Geographic Clusters ──► Priority Categories ──► Channel Strategy ──► Funnel Execution\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Section Navigation</h2>\n<p>| Sub-Page | Focus Area | Core Insight |<br/>| --- | --- | --- |<br/>| [Acquisition Goals](./acquisition_goals.md) | OKRs, volume targets & quality benchmarks | Weekly and monthly seller targets |<br/>| [Target Seller Profile](./target_seller_profile.md) | Ideal merchant characteristics | The exact criteria defining high-fit retail stores |<br/>| [Seller Categories](./seller_categories.md) | Category taxonomy & retail scopes | Approved retail categories for discovery |<br/>| [Target Locations](./target_locations.md) | Hyperlocal clustering & launch zones | Priority pin codes & commercial shopping streets |<br/>| [Seller Qualification Criteria](./seller_qualification_criteria.md) | Go / No-Go decision framework | How to qualify a store before outreach |<br/>| [Priority Seller Segments](./priority_seller_segments.md) | Phased category rollout plan | Where to concentrate current acquisition sprints |<br/>| [Acquisition Channels](./acquisition_channels.md) | Multi-channel sourcing mix | Google Maps, Instagram, Referrals & Local Hubs |<br/>| [Seller Acquisition Funnel](./seller_acquisition_funnel.md) | Funnel stages, math & velocity | Stage metrics from Identified to Active Seller |</p>\n<h2>Roles & Responsibilities</h2>\n<li><strong>Operations Lead:</strong> Sets quarterly OKRs, adjusts category priorities, and defines target location boundaries.</li>\n<li><strong>Squad 1 & 3 (Discovery):</strong> Enforce strict qualification criteria and geographic boundaries during sourcing.</li>\n<li><strong>Squad 2 (Outreach):</strong> Tailor messaging hooks to the designated priority retail segments.</li>\n<li><strong>Squad 5 (Analytics):</strong> Measure stage conversion rates across categories and locations to inform strategic adjustments.</li>\n<h2>Best Practices</h2>\n<li>Always maintain geographic density: prioritize signing 10 shops on the same commercial street over 10 shops scattered across the city.</li>\n<li>Focus on shops carrying search-driven items with high availability search urgency (electronics, sports, gifts, apparel).</li>\n<li>Track conversion differentials between Google Maps and Instagram channels weekly.</li>\n<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>\n<li>Prospecting outside designated target pin codes, creating discovery dead zones.</li>\n<li>Lowering qualification standards just to hit raw lead volume quotas.</li>\n<li>Reaching out to service-only businesses (salons, dry cleaners) that do not sell physical products.</li>\n<h2>Quick Summary</h2>\n<li>Strategy guides our team to focus on high-density, search-driven local retail stores.</li>\n<li>We target specific geographic clusters (pin codes) to ensure rapid local discovery and store density.</li>\n<li>The Target Seller Profile (TSP) defines our ideal merchant attributes and operational readiness.</li>\n<li>Sourcing occurs through targeted Google Maps sweeps, curated Instagram discovery, and merchant referrals.</li>\n<li>The entire team executes against a standardized 6-stage acquisition funnel.</li>\n<h2>Related Pages</h2>\n<li>[Acquisition Goals](./acquisition_goals.md)</li>\n<li>[Target Seller Profile](./target_seller_profile.md)</li>\n<li>[Seller Qualification Criteria](./seller_qualification_criteria.md)</li>\n<li>[Google Maps Research](../04_seller_discovery/google_maps_research.md)</li>\n<li>[Instagram Research](../04_seller_discovery/instagram_research.md)</li>\n<h2>Resources</h2>\n<li>[Vipto City Expansion Roadmap [To be defined by Vipto]]</li>",
