    "content": "<h1>README</h1>\n<h1>🚀 Start Here — Overview & Navigation</h1>\n<h2>PAGE INFORMATION</h2>\n<li><strong>Page Name:</strong> Start Here — Topic Overview</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Provide an overarching entry point and table of contents for the Start Here onboarding section of Vipto Seller Acquisition.</li>\n<li><strong>Section:</strong> 1. 🚀 Start Here</li>\n<h2>Overview</h2>\n<p>Welcome to the central onboarding portal of the <strong>Vipto Seller Acquisition Playbook</strong>. Vipto is a hyperlocal product discovery platform that enables customers to find products in nearby physical stores before visiting them in person. Our guiding principle is: <strong>“Search Online. Confirm Availability. Buy Offline.”</strong> This section equips every new Product Operations intern with a complete understanding of how our acquisition team operates, why onboarding local merchants is vital to Vipto, and how our 11-person team is organized into 5 squads.</p>\n<h2>Why This Matters</h2>\n<p>Local brick-and-mortar retail stores carry exceptional products but remain invisible online, while customers waste hours visiting multiple shops to find in-stock items (like a laptop charger or specific sports gear). By acquiring and onboarding local shop owners onto the Vipto Seller App, your daily work builds the verified digital catalog that powers instant product discovery and real-time availability confirmation across neighborhood shopping districts.</p>\n<h2>Objectives</h2>\n<li>Understand the core mission and unique discovery-first value proposition of Vipto.</li>\n<li>Master the end-to-end seller acquisition flow from discovery to active catalog status.</li>\n<li>Learn the structure of the 11-person Product Operations team across 5 specialized squads.</li>\n<li>Configure all operational tools (HubSpot, WhatsApp Business, Instagram, Google Maps, Notion).</li>\n<li>Complete all onboarding milestones detailed in the First Week Checklist.</li>\n<h2>How It Works</h2>\n<p>The Start Here section is structured as a progressive roadmap. Team members should review these pages in order before handling live merchant leads in HubSpot or conducting outreach.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">1. Welcome & Mission ──&gt; 2. Acquisition Flow ──&gt; 3. Team & Squads ──&gt; 4. Tools Setup ──&gt; 5. Week 1 Execution\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Section Navigation</h2>\n<p>| Sub-Page | Focus Area | Primary Audience |<br/>| --- | --- | --- |<br/>| [Welcome to Seller Acquisition](./welcome_to_seller_acquisition.md) | Introduction to team culture, mission, and seller acquisition impact | All Interns |<br/>| [Our Mission](./our_mission.md) | High-level goals, merchant empowerment, and product discovery vision | All Interns |<br/>| [How the System Works](./how_the_system_works.md) | The request-based discovery engine and operational dynamics | All Interns |<br/>| [Complete Seller Acquisition Flow](./complete_seller_acquisition_flow.md) | Step-by-step pipeline from research to active catalog | All Interns |<br/>| [Team Structure](./team_structure.md) | 5 squads, 11 interns, and functional role breakdown | All Interns |<br/>| [Squad Responsibilities](./squad_responsibilities.md) | Day-to-day charters and handoffs for each squad | All Interns |<br/>| [Tools We Use](./tools_we_use.md) | Setup, configuration, and security guidelines for tools | All Interns |<br/>| [First Week Checklist](./first_week_checklist.md) | Day-by-day onboarding and verification checklist | New Interns |</p>\n<h2>Roles & Responsibilities</h2>\n<li><strong>New Interns:</strong> Read and review all documentation within the first 48 hours; complete tool setups.</li>\n<li><strong>Squad Leads / Mentors:</strong> Review checklist progress on Day 3 and Day 5; conduct tool walkthroughs.</li>\n<li><strong>Operations Lead:</strong> Maintain and update this documentation as workflows evolve.</li>\n<h2>Best Practices</h2>\n<li>Bookmark this directory and reference it whenever you encounter edge cases in CRM or communication.</li>\n<li>Always remember Vipto’s core model: we are a product discovery platform driving offline foot traffic, not a delivery app.</li>\n<li>Never make assumptions regarding merchant policies—consult the playbooks.</li>\n<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>\n<li>Describing Vipto as a multi-day e-commerce shipping platform or food delivery service.</li>\n<li>Skipping foundational reading to start messaging shop owners prematurely.</li>\n<li>Operating without properly configuring WhatsApp Business or HubSpot tags.</li>\n<h2>Quick Summary</h2>\n<li>Vipto is a hyperlocal product discovery platform: <em>“Search Online. Confirm Availability. Buy Offline.”</em></li>\n<li>Our mission is to digitize local store inventory so nearby customers can check real-time stock before visiting.</li>\n<li>11 Product Operations interns are organized into 5 specialized squads to run a tight acquisition pipeline.</li>\n<li>All operations rely on connected tools: Google Maps, Instagram, HubSpot CRM, and WhatsApp Business.</li>\n<li>Complete your Day 1 to Day 5 checklist items to transition into live operations smoothly.</li>\n<h2>Related Pages</h2>\n<li>[Welcome to Seller Acquisition](./welcome_to_seller_acquisition.md)</li>\n<li>[Our Mission](./our_mission.md)</li>\n<li>[What is Vipto?](../02_learn_vipto/what_is_vipto.md)</li>\n<li>[Complete Seller Acquisition Flow](./complete_seller_acquisition_flow.md)</li>\n<li>[Team Structure](./team_structure.md)</li>\n<h2>Resources</h2>\n<li>[HubSpot CRM Documentation](https://knowledge.hubspot.com/)</li>\n<li>[WhatsApp Business Overview](https://business.whatsapp.com/)</li>\n<li>[Notion Guides](https://www.notion.so/help)</li>",
    "excerpt": "README\n\n 🚀 Start Here — Overview & Navigation\n\n PAGE INFORMATION\n\n- Page Name: Start Here — Topic Overview\n- Purpose: Provide an overarching entry point and t",
