    "id": "disc_readme_68",
    "workspaceId": "vipto-workspace",
    "spaceId": "space_seller_disc",
    "parentId": null,
    "title": "README",
    "slug": "readme",
    "icon": "🔍",
    "content": "<h1>README</h1>\n<h1>🔎 Seller Discovery — Overview & Roadmap</h1>\n<h2>PAGE INFORMATION</h2>\n<li><strong>Page Name:</strong> Seller Discovery — Topic Overview</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Provide an overarching roadmap and standard operating procedures for discovering, researching, and qualifying potential sellers online.</li>\n<li><strong>Section:</strong> 4. 🔎 Seller Discovery</li>\n<h2>Overview</h2>\n<p><strong>Seller Discovery</strong> is the top-of-funnel research engine for Vipto. This section consolidates all methodologies, search techniques, qualification heuristics, duplicate prevention protocols, and quality standards used by Squad 1 (Google Maps Research) and Squad 3 (Instagram Discovery) to find high-potential local merchants.</p>\n<h2>Why This Matters</h2>\n<p>The quality of our entire acquisition pipeline is determined right here. If discovery interns source invalid phone numbers, closed businesses, or out-of-scope services, downstream outreach squads waste hours sending dead messages. Pristine, highly qualified discovery feeds our growth engine with high-converting opportunities.</p>\n<h2>Objectives</h2>\n<li>Master Google Maps geo-spatial search techniques, keyword matrices, and business verification.</li>\n<li>Master Instagram social discovery, hashtag monitoring, and visual brand auditing.</li>\n<li>Execute mandatory duplicate checking protocols before adding any lead to HubSpot CRM.</li>\n<li>Collect all required standardized data points in the Lead Research Checklist.</li>\n<li>Classify lead quality (High / Medium / Low) with 100% accuracy.</li>\n<h2>How It Works</h2>\n<p>Discovery operates as a dual-channel mining and filtering operation:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">┌─────────────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────────────┐\n│   GOOGLE MAPS (Squad 1) │       │   INSTAGRAM (Squad 3)   │\n│   Geo-spatial sweeps    │       │   Hashtags & visual feeds│\n└────────────┬────────────┘       └────────────┬────────────┘\n             │                                 │\n             └────────────────┬────────────────┘\n                              │\n                              ▼\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ MANDATORY DUPLICATE CHECK (HubSpot Search by Phone & Name)│\n└─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                              │\n                              ▼\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ LEAD QUALIFICATION & SCORING (TSP & 5-Point Rubric)       │\n└─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                              │\n                              ▼\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ STANDARDIZED HUBSPOT ENTRY (Assigned to Outreach Queue)   │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Section Navigation</h2>\n<p>| Sub-Page | Focus Area | Core Insight |<br/>| --- | --- | --- |<br/>| [Google Maps Research](./google_maps_research.md) | Geo-spatial search, keyword matrices & data extraction | Step-by-step Google Maps mining SOP |<br/>| [Instagram Research](./instagram_research.md) | Social discovery, hashtag trees & aesthetic auditing | Finding local creators on Instagram |<br/>| [Lead Research Checklist](./lead_research_checklist.md) | Standardized data collection schema | Mandatory fields for every lead |<br/>| [Duplicate Checking](./duplicate_checking.md) | Deduplication protocols & search queries | Preventing double outreach and CRM clutter |<br/>| [Lead Quality Guidelines](./lead_quality_guidelines.md) | Tier A / B / C evaluation rubric | Grading lead potential and responsiveness |</p>\n<h2>Roles & Responsibilities</h2>\n<li><strong>Intern 1 (Seller Research - Squad 1):</strong> Executes daily Google Maps sweeps in assigned pin codes.</li>\n<li><strong>Intern 2 (Lead Qualification - Squad 1):</strong> Audits leads against TSP and performs duplicate verification.</li>\n<li><strong>Intern 3 (CRM Manager - Squad 1):</strong> Ingests verified records into HubSpot and routes them to outreach queues.</li>\n<li><strong>Intern 6 (Instagram Discovery - Squad 3):</strong> Discovers, evaluates, and qualifies social-first brands on Instagram.</li>\n<h2>Best Practices</h2>\n<li>Never enter a lead into HubSpot without searching by both Phone Number and Business Name first.</li>\n<li>Always verify that the phone number is a 10-digit mobile line capable of receiving WhatsApp messages.</li>\n<li>Capture a direct link to the business profile (Google Maps URL or Instagram profile URL) for outreach context.</li>\n<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>\n<li>Relying on generic keywords (e.g., <em>“shops”</em>) instead of targeted long-tail queries (e.g., <em>“artisan sourdough bakery 100ft road”</em>).</li>\n<li>Forgetting to check business hours or recent review dates, resulting in closed shops being contacted.</li>\n<li>Logging unverified landline numbers (e.g., <code>080-...</code>) into mobile phone fields.</li>\n<h2>Quick Summary</h2>\n<li>Seller Discovery mines and filters prospective merchants across Google Maps and Instagram.</li>\n<li>Squad 1 owns Google Maps; Squad 3 owns Instagram discovery.</li>\n<li>Every lead must pass duplicate checks and meet Target Seller Profile standards.</li>\n<li>Discovery interns collect standardized data fields before passing leads to HubSpot.</li>\n<li>High-quality discovery directly drives high outreach response rates and rapid onboarding.</li>\n<h2>Related Pages</h2>\n<li>[Google Maps Research](./google_maps_research.md)</li>\n<li>[Instagram Research](./instagram_research.md)</li>\n<li>[Lead Research Checklist](./lead_research_checklist.md)</li>\n<li>[Target Seller Profile](../03_seller_acquisition_strategy/target_seller_profile.md)</li>\n<li>[How to Add a Seller in HubSpot](../05_seller_leads_and_crm/how_to_add_a_seller.md)</li>\n<h2>Resources</h2>\n<li>[Google Maps Platform](https://www.google.com/maps)</li>\n<li>[Instagram Web Search](https://www.instagram.com/)</li>",
