    "title": "Team Working Principles & Flexibility",
    "slug": "team-working-principles-flexibility",
    "icon": "🔬",
    "content": "<h1>Team Working Principles & Flexibility</h1>\n<h1></h1>\n<p>Vipto follows a <strong>trust-based and flexible working culture</strong> built around ownership, communication, collaboration, and meaningful contribution. We want team members to have the freedom to manage their work comfortably while maintaining the reliability required to build a real product.</p>\n<h3><strong>Build Day</strong></h3>\n<p>Our primary in-person collaboration day is <strong>Sunday, from 10:30 AM to 3:00 PM</strong>. Build Day is intended for focused collaboration, product development, engineering collaboration, onboarding, discussions, and team interaction.</p>\n<p>Team members are free to choose where they sit and how they organize their workspace during the day. We do not require a fixed seating arrangement or constant group interaction.</p>\n<p>If you are unable to attend a <strong>Build Day due to a genuine and unavoidable reason</strong>, please email [<strong>ayush.vipto@gmail.com</strong>](mailto:ayush.vipto@gmail.com) in advance and mention the reason.</p>\n<p>Once informed, you can attend the Build Day <strong>online</strong> and continue working on your assigned tasks remotely. Please make sure to stay updated with any important discussions or announcements from the Build Day.</p>\n<h3><strong>Weekday Work</strong></h3>\n<p>During the weekdays, team members generally contribute remotely according to their assigned responsibilities and ongoing work. The expected contribution is typically <strong>around 3–5 hours</strong>, while the exact timing can remain flexible depending on the work being handled.</p>\n<p>You are not expected to remain continuously online. What matters is that you remain reasonably reachable when coordination is required, communicate delays or blockers, and complete the responsibilities you have taken ownership of.</p>\n<h3><strong>Lunch & Breaks</strong></h3>\n<p>Lunch and normal breaks are completely flexible. You may have lunch whenever convenient and with whoever you prefer. There is no mandatory team lunch.</p>\n<p>Occasionally, Vipto may organize <strong>optional team lunches or informal team activities</strong> so members can spend time together outside regular engineering work.</p>\n<h3><strong>Our Principle</strong></h3>\n<p>Vipto gives team members freedom because we expect <strong>responsibility in return</strong>.</p>\n<p>If you are unavailable, communicate. If you are blocked, ask. If you commit to something, take ownership of it. If plans change, keep your lead informed.</p>",
    "excerpt": "Team Working Principles & Flexibility\n\n \n\nVipto follows a trust-based and flexible working culture built around ownership, communication, collaboration, and me",
